cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If OpenDubStage helped a production, a paper or a course, please cite it with the metadata below."
title: "OpenDubStage: open tools for documentary and film sound post-production"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "The OpenDubStage contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/gothicpixie/opendubstage"
url: "https://github.com/gothicpixie/opendubstage"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0.dev0
date-released: "2026-10-13"
keywords:
  - audio post-production
  - documentary sound
  - dialogue editing
  - spectral repair
  - loudness
  - EBU R128
  - ITU-R BS.1770
  - music ducking
  - foley
abstract: >-
  Command-line and Python tools for sound post-production on documentaries, films, podcasts and radio:
  spectral repair and de-rumble for dialogue, long-term-average-spectrum EQ matching between voices,
  speech-keyed music ducking and posts, J- and L-cut transitions on a cue sheet, a broadcast-style mix QC
  pass (BS.1770-4 integrated loudness, true peak, loudness range, dead air, clicks, level jumps, masking)
  and rule-governed sound for still photographs. Every default cites a standard, a delivery specification
  or a measurement, and every behaviour is pinned by a synthetic test.
